// gdpr — EU General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679
//
// The law: personal data may leave the EEA only for a country with an EU
// adequacy decision (Art. 45) or under appropriate safeguards such as
// standard contractual clauses (Art. 46). Processors must give sufficient
// guarantees of security (Art. 28, Art. 32).
//
// This pack: everything runs in the EEA or an adequate country, on offers
// with a contract and a SOC 2 / ISO 27001 audit (T2 or better).
//
// Not covered: transfers under contractual clauses or binding corporate
// rules (contracts, not locations), and the EU–US Data Privacy Framework,
// which covers only certified US organisations. If you rely on either,
// write your own policy instead of importing this one.
//
// Use `import "gdpr"`. Not legal advice.

policy gdpr {
  residency = gdpr-adequate
  min_trust = T2
}
